QuestGuidance.Register("en",359,{
[11457]="7007179E\n1\tGather rotting flowers (total: 8)\030Gather rotting berries (total: 6)\030Find missing pages\tTálbiral needs help gathering flowers and berries near Laivárth so that he can check how the blight is affecting them as well as recovering the missing pages of his notebook.\n2\tReturn to Tálbiral in Laivárth\tBring the gathered flowers, berries, and missing notebook pages back to Tálbiral in Laivárth.\n",
[11458]="70062E80\n1\tCollect meat from the boars of the South Downs (total: 6)\030Collect hides from the lynx of the South Downs (total: 4)\tBoars and lynxes of the South Downs can provide the supplies for which Haerandir has asked.\n2\tBring the boar-meat and lynx hides to Haerandir outside Haudh Nirui\tHaerandir is outside Haudh Nirui, on the South Downs.\n3\tBring the boar-meat and lynx hides to Sirvellon at Sírlond\tSirvellon is at Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.\n",
[11459]="70054663\n1\tCollect the Ranger supplies\tThe crate of Ranger supplies can be found in Echad Taerdim. You should collect the supplies to take to the Rangers in Cirith Ungol.\n2\tDeliver supplies to the resting Ranger\030Deliver supplies to the famished Ranger\030Deliver supplies to the tracking Ranger\030Deliver supplies to the ill Ranger\030Deliver supplies to the nervous Ranger\tRangers of Ithilien can be found in the western cliffs of Cirith Ungol. You should deliver supplies to any Rangers you find. Mírthel said there were five.\n3\tTalk to Mírthel\tMírthel can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Mírthel.\n",
[11460]="70062D71\n1\tDNT - Return to the master of the lash in Urugarth\tDNT - You stared at the boxes. You think you may have counted them. Do you know how to count? There are likely more than enough. When the master of the lash asks, you just look confident. Get back and tell the master of the lash there are enough supplies.\n",
[11461]="7005A72F\n1\tDestroy provisions at Târ-kútoz\tThe Orc camp Târ-kútoz guards the watch-tower Atrad-zarakh. Destroying their provisions would force the Orcs to use resources to secure more food.\n2\tThe Orc camp Târ-kútoz guards the watch-tower Atrad-zarakh. Destroying their provisions would force the Orcs to use resources to secure more food.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed the Orcs' provisions at Târ-kútoz.\n",
[11462]="70071B30\n1\tTalk to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur\tTekâmi has asked you to go to Khanâg Gur and speak with their leader on her behalf about the possibility of a business partnership.\n2\tHelp the Ordâkhai 'lose' their rations (total: 6)\tYou went to Khanâg Gur to ask Halshûm if he wanted to do business with Tekâmi. He did not, but he will find someone who does if you do something for him. He wants you to go to Kôth Rau and take back the rations that he recently sold to them, so that they will need to buy more. Kôth Rau is in southern An Shêru.\n3\tBring the rations to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur\tYou went to Khanâg Gur to ask Halshûm if he wanted to do business with Tekâmi. He did not, but he will find someone who does if you do something for him. You went to Kôth Rau and took back the ration crates he recently sold to them, so that they will need to buy more. You should return to Halshûm at Khanâg Gur in central An Shêru.\n4\tBring the rations to Nabatínu in Gadim-ûn\tAfter helping Halshûm, he gave you the name of a merchant in Zajâna, Zarzûmir, who will do business with Tekâmi. He did not want the Ordâkhai rations that you helped the soldiers of Kôth Rau 'lose' and said you can do whatever you want with them. You should give them to the Jatsakóri in north-eastern An Shêru, as they are always in need of supplies.\n5\tTalk to Zarzûmir in Zajâna\tAfter helping Halshûm, he gave you the name of a merchant in Zajâna, Zarzûmir, who will do business with Tekâmi. You first gave the Ordâkhai rations to the Jatsakóri at Gadim-ûn, and should now go to Zajâna in search of Zarzûmir, who is said to always be in one of the markets.\n6\tReturn to Tekâmi in Jiret-menêsh\tYou met with Zarzûmir in Zajâna, and he agreed to trade with Tekâmi. You should return to Jiret-menêsh and tell Tekâmi of your success.\n",
[11463]="7006F088\n1\tGather crate of swords\030Gather crate of spears\030Gather crate of bows\tSome new recruits have volunteered in Iridír after news of the attacks. Bâdarul has asked that you help supply them with weapons so they can begin their training. Gather supplies of weapons from crates nearby.\n2\tArm recruits with swords (total: 4)\030Arm recruits with spears (total: 4)\030Arm recruits with bows (total: 3)\tArm the recruits in Iridír with the weapons they desire so that they can begin their training.\n3\tReturn to Bâdarul\tReturn to Bâdarul in Iridír and inform him that you have armed the new recruits and they are not ready to begin training.\n",
[11464]="7002EE42\n1\tTalk to Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tLady Góda stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Ingbert has asked you to speak with his mother, Lady Góda, and learn the heart of her arguments.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert stands near Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should consider Góda's argument. If her reasoning seems preferable to Ingmar's, you should speak with Reeve Ingbert on her behalf.\n",
[11465]="7002EE41\n1\tTalk to Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tLord Ingmar stands near Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Ingbert has bidden you speak with Ingmar regarding his plan, to learn whether the greater wisdom is to follow his son into battle.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngbert stands near Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. If you believe that Ingmar's reasoning is greater than Góda's, you should bring your support of his plan to Ingbert.\n",
[11466]="70061F79\n1\tObtain the supporter pack bestowal object\tEnjoy your reward for being a supporter.\n",
[11467]="70061F7A\n1\tObtain the supporter pack bestowal object\tEnjoy your reward for being a supporter.\n",
[11468]="70061F81\n1\tObtain the supporter pack bestowal object\tEnjoy your reward for being a supporter.\n",
[11469]="7001BFC8\n1\tTalk to Cwendreda at Dol Vaeg\tMake your way to the ruins of Dol Vaeg and speak with Cwendreda. The ruins are east and north of the Great East Road on a high hill. Frideric the Elder, in an effort to further garner your help for the Eglain, sent you to Dol Vaeg to assist Cwendreda.\n",
[11470]="7006B71B\n1\tTalk to Dalagín\tYou should talk to the Dumûri captain, Dalagín, on the south side of Iridír, near the river.\n",
[11471]="7000982A\n1\tFind the solution to the riddle\tThe treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed: \"From this beach, you can see Rantost, A short swim across the water.\" You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.\n",
[11472]="7000B98A\n1\tBring pipe-weed pouch to someone in Rivendell\tSomeone in Rivendell, north of Tâl Bruinen, may know how the barrel of pipe-weed came to rest off the road in the wilderness. You found a barrel of pipe-weed in the wilderness and have taken a pouch from it to show someone in nearby Rivendell.\n",
[11473]="7005F865\n1\tExplore Glittengrof with Spall\tGlittengrof can be found to the south-west of Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Spall has asked you to join him in exploring Glittengrof. You should travel to Glittengrof.\n2\tTalk to Spall\tSpall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn. You have begun your survey of Glittengrof and it appears Spall wishes to speak to you. You should talk to Spall. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n3\tCollect broken crystal shards in Glittengrof (total: 12)\tBroken crystal shards can be found in Glittengrof in Gloomingtarn. Spall has asked you to collect broken crystal shards from Glittengrof.\n4\tDeliver the broken crystal shards to Spall\tSpall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn. You have collected a number of broken crystal shards in Glittengrof. You should deliver them to Spall. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n",
[11474]="7005F864\n1\tExplore Ormgren with Spall\tOrmgren can be found to the east of Watchers' Roost across Durthuzâram in Gloomingtarn. Spall has asked you to join him in exploring Ormgren. You should travel to Ormgren.\n2\tTalk to Spall\tSpall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn. You have begun your survey of Ormgren and it appears Spall wishes to speak to you. You should talk to Spall. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n3\tCollected glow-worm gizzards from glow-worms in Ormgren (total: 12)\tGlow-worm gizzards can be harvested from adult glow-worms in Ormgren. Spall has asked you to extract glow-worm gizzards from the glow-worms inhabiting Ormgren.\n4\tDeliver the glow-worm gizzards to Spall\tSpall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn. You have collected a number of glow-worm gizzards in Ormgren. You should deliver them to Spall. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n",
[11475]="70048C83\n1\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found in his hideout. You should talk to Viznak when you are ready to go.\n2\tSurvey the eastern side of Seregost\030Survey central Seregost\030Survey the western side of Seregost\tSeregost can be found at the northern end of Agarnaith. You should survey locations of Seregost's walls. If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.\n3\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be called with the goblin-caller. You should talk to Viznak.\n4\tComplete: A Bad Plan\tViznak has a few ideas for getting into Seregost. You should complete quests for Viznak. If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.\n5\tComplete: Another Bad Plan\tViznak has a few ideas for getting into Seregost. You should complete quests for Viznak. If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.\n6\tComplete: Yet Another Bad Plan\tViznak has a few ideas for getting into Seregost. You should complete quests for Viznak. If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.\n7\tFind a suitable location for Viznak to climb up\tSomewhere along Seregost's walls should be a suitable location for the climb. You should find a suitable location for Viznak to climb up. If Viznak wanders off, you can call him back with the goblin-caller.\n8\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be called with the goblin-caller. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[11476]="70047A59\n1\tSurvey the Black Gate\030Survey the base of Narchost\030Survey the tower of Narchost\030Survey the base of Carchost\030Survey the tower of Carchost\tGood vantage points can be found around the Slag-hills. You should survey the Black Gate and the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tReturn to Thurindol\tYou should return to Thurindol, who can be found at the small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[11477]="70059324\n1\tTalk to Nellie Boskins\030Talk to Guardsman Otley\030Talk to Aggy Digweed\030Talk to Giles Chadwick\tAggy Digweed, Guardsman Otley, Giles Chadwick, and Nellie Boskins can all be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aggy Digweed, Guardsman Otley, Giles Chadwick, and Nellie Boskins as soon as you are able.\n2\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n3\tScout Norwarden\030Scout Sutwarden\030Scout Overwine Hall\030Scout the Old Bluff-house\030Scout Marl's Crossing\030Defeat Orcs and brigands in the Wildwood (total: 12)\tMarl's Crossing, Norwarden, Old Bluff-house, Overwine Hall, and Sutwarden can all be found in the Wildwood. You should scout the Wildwood for the Woodcutter's Brotherhood and defeat any brigands and Orcs that you find along the way.\n4\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found in Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n",
